      "side": 1,
      "message": "A `#[no_mangle]` static in a library crate is one global name for the whole binary. A host that links two semver-incompatible vali-runtime versions (during an upgrade, say) fails to link with a duplicate symbol. Putting the version in the name (`VALI_DEBUG_STATES_3`) avoids that, and lets an extension that doesn\u0027t know the version say so before it reads anything. It\u0027s an edge case, so only if it\u0027s cheap.",
      "revId": "2ee5a2aeb47eaf4e7f70f3af4fcea6433b697500",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
