      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T17:37:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The bound counts *running* records, not records visited. A list whose `next` pointers loop through records that aren\u0027t running, which only corrupted memory could produce, would spin the debugger for ever. Counting every record visited (`seen +\u003d 1` per step, stop at the bound) keeps the guard doing what it\u0027s for.",
      "revId": "2ee5a2aeb47eaf4e7f70f3af4fcea6433b697500",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
